<in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock contextRef="OneD">(1)The above financial results for the Q1 ended 30.06.23 in respect of TTK Healthcare Limited have been reviewed by the AC at its meeting held on 31.07.23 &amp; approved by the BOD of the Co. at its meeting held on 01.08.23 at the RO of the Co. also, with the provision of VC(2)The Statutory Auditors of the Co. have carried out Limited Review of the above Unaudited Financial Results in terms of R.33 of the SEBI (LODR) R., 2015.(3)(a)Profit from Discontinued Operations (pertaining to previous year):(i)Gain on sale of undertaking:During the Q1 of FY22-23, the necessary formalities for transfer of the Human Pharma Division (HPD) of the Co. were completed &amp; the HPD  stood transferred as a going concern on slump sale basis, for a consideration of Rs.80500 lakhs (final consideration of Rs.80281.54 lakhs after working capital &amp; other customary adjustments) to BSV Pharma P. L. w.e.f 09.05.22.The consideration for the transfer was 74% cash (Rs.59442.51 lakhs) &amp; 26% in the form of Eq of the buying entity. The terms of transfer also provided for purchase of the aforesaid 26% Equity Shares held by the Co. in BSV, by Bharat Serums &amp; Vaccines Limited or its nominees, after they obtain necessary regulatory clearances at the issue price.During the Q3 of FY22-23, the above shares were transferred to M/s Bharat Serums &amp; Vaccines L. &amp; the consid. of Rs.20839.03 lakhs for the shares was received by the Co.The gain on sale of this Undertaking amounted to Rs.76,429.45 lakhs (after providing for Rs.1,500 lakhs towards contingencies of which Co. had incurred expenses amounting to Rs.266.58 lakhs till 31.03.23).(ii)Profit from HPD Operations:The total income of HPD up to the date of sale (i.e.) 09.05.22 was Rs.2240.57 lakhs (including reversal of provision made towards damaged / expired stock returns in the earlier years amounting to Rs.1132.29 lakhs which was no longer required) &amp; its total expenses were Rs.1026.10 lakhs resulting in a net profit of Rs.1214.47 lakhs.(b)Tax expense of Discontinued Operations:The tax expense on sale of HPD was Rs.17835.48 lakhs (i.e. Long Term Capital Gain tax expense on the above transfer amounting to Rs.17769.26 lakhs &amp; Deferred Tax expenses of Rs.66.22 lakhs).The tax expense on the profit for the year ended 31.03.23 from the operations of HPD was Rs.303.94 lakhs.(4)Implementation of the Code of Social Security 2020, which was likely to impact the contributions by the Co. towards Provident Fund, Gratuity &amp; other related areas has been deferred by the Government beyond 01.04.21. However, the Co. based on the initial assessment made a provision for Rs.350 lakhs in the Q4 of FY20-21 &amp; proposes to take further appropriate action after the Rules are made applicable.(5)The Co.'s Promoters made an Initial Public Announcement on 05.04.23 in accordance with R. 8 of the SEBI (Delisting of Equity Shares) Regulations, 2021, to acquire all Equity Shares aggregating to 3594493 Eq. Sh. of Rs.10/- each that are held by the Public Shareholders of the Co., either individually / collectively, or together with other members of the Promoter Group, as the case may be; &amp; consequently, voluntarily delist the Eq. Sh. of the Co. from the Stock Exchanges where the Equity Shares are presently listed (i.e.) BSE &amp; NSE.  However, as the stipulated threshold limit of 90% of the PSC of the Co. as per the Delisting Regulations was not met through the offer from the Public Shareholders, the delisting proposal was not successful.(6)The figures for the Quarter ended 31.03.23 are the balancing figures between the Audited Figures in respect of the full FY &amp; the published year to date figures upto the end of the Q3 of the relevant financial year which were subjected to Limited Review.(7)The previous period's/year's figures have been regrouped &amp; reclassified, wherever necessary to conform to the current period's/year's presentation.(8)The full financial results for the Q1 ended 30.06.23 are available on the website of BSE, NSE &amp; of the Co.</in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock>
